    {
      "id": "claim_c4c59117e8ca45f8ac4c04c8110f5c8d",
      "statement": "The main local infrastructure definition is `services/main-backend/docker-compose.yml`, which starts Postgres on `127.0.0.1:5432`, Redis on `127.0.0.1:6379`, a `server` container mapped from host port `18080` to container port `8080`, and a separate `worker` container that runs `/worker`; the root `infra/docker-compose.yml` is currently empty.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://infra/docker-compose.yml",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://services/main-backend/docker-compose.yml#L1-L97",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f86c82ed9b5c4ba9522e7ac2591ee46dca47424e181f5644ebc955e600527be8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_153d0cd3260f42f5bb580c78d42830cb",
      "statement": "The repository standardizes local backend access on `http://localhost:18080`; the README explicitly says this avoids a Windows and WSL `wslrelay` conflict on `localhost:8080`, while the backend config defaults `PORT` to `18080` and the Docker stack maps host `18080` to container `8080`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L24-L47",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:affcdead05e6aab8babb97a867f423f5d644d120a45ca96eb5f80dee9a4e3e28:"
